        "Criterion 1.2": {
            "analysis": "The assistant defined a composite risk score S using six factors: profit margin (lower = riskier), profit CV (higher = riskier), upstream HHI (higher = riskier), downstream HHI (higher = riskier), credit rating ordinal (A=1 to D=4), and default flag (Yes=1). Weights sum to 100% (20%, 20%, 15%, 15%, 20%, 10%). Directionality is clearly described. The analysis matches Path 1.2.A (Weighted aggregation and validation).",
            "best_path_analysis": {
