{
    "Requirement 1": {
        "Criterion 1.1": {
            "analysis": "The assistant did not construct the sample as specified in the rubric. They did not deduplicate to the latest record, filter for job_stage='technical interview', nor produce the required sample sizes (2,512 interview-level, 964 application-level). They used a broader sample (all interviews with technical_score not null) and merged application and interview data without the specified filtering and deduplication. They defined a 'prestigious_company' flag but used a broader list than the rubric's mapping (FAANG, Unicorn, BigTech, Other). They reported different sample sizes (7,172 merged sample, 4,218 prestigious). Therefore, the assistant did not meet the completeness, precision, or conclusion sub-standards for Path 1.1.A.",
            "criterion_type": "Completeness, Precision, Conclusion",
            "score": 0
        },
        "Criterion 1.2": {
            "analysis": "The assistant's analysis does not closely match any of the prescribed paths (ANOVA, Kruskal-Wallis, Permutation). They performed an OLS regression controlling for multiple factors to test the effect of 'prestigious_company' on technical score, reporting a coefficient of 0.175 (p=0.022). This is a multivariate approach rather than the pairwise significance testing required in Standard 1.2. Since no path fits, I will reason independently based on domain knowledge. The assistant provided a controlled analysis showing a small but significant effect of company background, but did not perform the specific group comparisons or report the required statistics. Their analysis addresses the spirit of evaluating differences but lacks the granular group comparisons and statistical tests outlined in the rubric.",
            "best_path_analysis": {
                "Criterion 1.2.notfound.1": {
                    "analysis": "The assistant did not construct the required application-level sample with the four company groups, nor did they perform ANOVA or pairwise tests. They did not report group means or statistical test results matching any path. Therefore, they did not meet the completeness requirement.",
                    "criterion_type": "Completeness",
                    "score": 0
                },
                "Criterion 1.2.notfound.2": {
                    "analysis": "The assistant's regression results (coefficient 0.175, p=0.022) are not comparable to the rubric's anchors (group means, ANOVA F, pairwise differences). They provided some raw averages for FAANG companies but not for the defined groups. Precision is lacking.",
                    "criterion_type": "Precision",
                    "score": 0
                },
                "Criterion 1.2.notfound.3": {
