                    "criterion_type": "Conclusion",
                    "score": 1
                }
            },
            "score": 1
        },
        "total_score": 1
    },
    "Requirement 2": {
        "Criterion 2.1": {
            "analysis": "The assistant performed an OLS regression (Model 1) controlling for company background (prestigious flag), education (university_tier), experience (years_of_experience, skill_count), gender, and race. This aligns with the spirit of Path 2.1.A but does not match exactly: they used a binary 'prestigious_company' variable instead of the four-category company_group with BigTech as reference, and omitted several control variables (gpa, interviewer characteristics, interview difficulty, time, day). Their sample size (7,172) is larger than the rubric's 2,512. Coefficients differ: they found prestigious_company = 0.175 (p=0.022), whereas Path 2.1.A shows negative non-significant coefficients for FAANG/Unicorn/Other vs BigTech. Since the model specification and results diverge significantly, no path matches perfectly. I will reason independently.",
